description:
A frame profiler records samples: each one a section name and how many microseconds it took. Write `summarise(samples)`, which returns one `Row` per name with:

- `name`;
- `count`: how many samples it had;
- `total`: the sum of its times;
- `worst`: its largest single time;
- `average`: `total / count`, as a `double`.

Rows are sorted by `total`, largest first; names with equal totals are sorted alphabetically.

```
{ "render", 9000 } { "physics", 3000 } { "render", 11000 } { "ai", 2000 }
-> render  count 2  total 20000  worst 11000  average 10000
   physics count 1  total 3000   worst 3000   average 3000
   ai      count 1  total 2000   worst 2000   average 2000
```

